# kgcache.conf.example
#
# Settings below show built-in defaults. Uncomment a setting to change it.
# Omitted settings keep their defaults. Extra examples are marked separately.
#
# Format: one directive per line, `directive value`. Blank lines and lines
# starting with `#` are ignored. Anything else must be a recognized
# directive with a value -- an unknown directive, a missing value, or a
# value outside the directive's accepted range all fail the server at
# startup with a message on stderr, rather than being silently ignored.
#
# Run with: ./zig-out/bin/kgcache path/to/kgcache.conf
# Use the supported directive names shown here. Old names such as
# num-databases, append-dirname, append-filename, and snapshot-path are
# rejected. Double quotes group file values; save "" clears rules.
# Names and yes/no or enum values are case-sensitive. Whitespace outside
# quotes is trimmed; string values can contain spaces. Inline comments are
# not supported. Repeated directives replace their value, except save,
# which collects rules in file order until save "" clears them.
# CLI overrides apply after this file: --port 7000 or --save '' to clear rules.
# The first CLI save replaces file rules; later CLI saves append or clear.
# See docs/CONFIGURATION.md for every CLI form and the supported Redis subset.

# Address the TCP server binds to.
# bind 127.0.0.1

# TCP port the server listens on. Range: 0 to 65535.
# Set 0 to let the OS select an available TCP port. Redis uses 0 to
# disable TCP instead. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md for this difference.
# port 6379

# Whether to set SO_REUSEADDR on the listening socket, which lets the
# server rebind quickly on restart instead of waiting for the OS to
# release the previous socket. yes or no.
# reuse-address yes

# Size, in bytes, of the per-connection read buffer. A request (or a
# pipelined batch of requests) larger than this is not yet supported.
# Range: 1 to the maximum usize value for this build.
# connection-buffer-size 1024

# Number of selectable databases: SELECT 0 through databases - 1.
# Range: 1 to 4294967295.
# databases 16

# Shared directory for snapshots and the AOF directory. It must already
# exist. A relative path resolves from the process working directory,
# not this config file's location. `~` is not expanded. Give the user
# running kgcache read and write access for persistence operations.
# dir .

# Snapshot filename within dir, loaded on startup when AOF is off and
# written by SAVE and BGSAVE. Must end in `.kgc` and contain no path
# separators. This is kgcache's own format, not Redis RDB.
# dbfilename dump.kgc
# Changing persistence paths or names does not move or convert old files.

# How often, in milliseconds, background work runs. This includes active
# expiration, AOF flushing, save checks, and child-process cleanup.
# Range: 1 to 9223372036854775807.
# cron-interval-ms 100

# Time budget, in milliseconds, the active-expiration worker spends per
# sweep before yielding, regardless of how many databases still have
# expirable keys left unchecked.
# Range: 1 to 127.
# active-expire-budget-ms 10

# Number of keys sampled per expiration batch, per database, before
# deciding whether to keep going or move to the next database.
# Range: 1 to 127.
# active-expire-batch-size 20

# If at least this percentage of a batch came back expired, immediately
# run another batch on the same database instead of moving on.
# Range: 1 to 100.
# active-expire-threshold-percent 25

# Prevent BGSAVE and BGREWRITEAOF from running at the same time. Keeping
# this on lowers memory use while a background child is running.
# exclusive-bg-persistence yes

# One or more rules for automatically triggering a background save
# (equivalent to BGSAVE) when enough writes have happened recently.
# Format: save <seconds> <changes> -- trigger if at least <changes>
# writes happened in the last <seconds> seconds since the last save.
# This directive may be repeated; if ANY rule's condition is met, a
# background save is triggered. With no `save` line at all (the
# default), automatic saving is disabled -- SAVE/BGSAVE still work
# on demand.
# Ranges: seconds 1 to 9223372036854775807; changes 1 to 4294967295.
# Use two values separated by spaces or tabs, or save "" to clear prior rules.
# save 3600 1
# save 300 100
# save 60 10000
# save ""

# Write each data change to an append-only file. yes or no.
# appendonly no

# AOF fsync policy: always, everysec, or no.
# appendfsync everysec

# Name of the AOF directory within dir. Must contain no path separators
# and cannot be `.` or `..`. kgcache creates and owns this directory when
# AOF is enabled; do not store other files in it.
# appenddirname appendonlydir

# Base name used to build AOF data and manifest file names.
# appendfilename appendonly.aof

# Rewrite the AOF after incremental data grows by this percentage.
# Set 0 to turn off automatic rewrites. Manual BGREWRITEAOF still works.
# Range: 0 to 4294967295.
# auto-aof-rewrite-percentage 100

# Do not start an automatic rewrite until the total AOF size reaches this
# many bytes. Values such as "64mb" are not accepted.
# Range: 0 to the maximum usize value for this build.
# auto-aof-rewrite-min-size 67108864

# If the last incremental file ends with an incomplete command, remove
# that command and continue loading. yes or no.
# aof-load-truncated yes

# Delay, in milliseconds, before retrying a failed automatic BGSAVE.
# Set 0 for no retry delay. Range: 0 to 9223372036854775807.
# bgsave-retry-delay-ms 5000

# Quoted alternatives (uncomment only the lines you need).
# The selected directory must already exist.
# port "7000"
# dir "data files"
# dbfilename "state file.kgc"
# dir "a\"b\\c"
# dir "\"data files\""
# save "60" "1"
# save ""
# Inside quotes, only \" and \\ are decoded. Inner spaces/tabs are kept.
# File single quotes are literal; shell quotes around CLI values are removed by the shell.
